---
import { Glossary } from '@/components/site/Glossary';
import { MethodStrip } from '@/components/site/Method';
import { passHatKTerm, terms } from '@/lib/glossary';

const columns = [
  terms.passRate,
  terms.passInterval,
  passHatKTerm('k'),
  terms.tasks,
  terms.errored,
  terms.testsCostLatency,
];
---

<MethodStrip scorer="tests" />
<p>
  A round closes once every system has run each task the same number of times, and the task's own
  tests grade each trial. A trial passes when its tests award the full reward, even after its agent
  timed out, and a trial whose tests never ran fails.
</p>
<p>
  A pass rate averages each task's share of passing trials, so every task counts once. Its 95%
  interval is an exact Clopper-Pearson interval that treats each task as one observation, since
  repeated trials of one task share its difficulty. It keeps its coverage near 100%, where pass
  rates often fall and approximate intervals come out too narrow for a family's few tasks. With
  several trials per task, pass^k gives the share of tasks where every trial passed.
</p>
<p>
  The board names the system with the top pass rate and any system that an exact paired sign test at
  the 5% level cannot separate from it. The test counts the shared tasks each system does better on,
  so with few tasks the top system has to win nearly every task where the two differ.
</p>
<Glossary heading="Column" entries={columns} />
